{"repositoryId":1166883340,"availability":"available","full":"ebalderasr/PulseGrowth","name":"PulseGrowth","description":"Browser-based growth kinetics and q-rate calculator for two-point mammalian cell culture sampling.","category":"Other","language":"JavaScript","stars":0,"forks":0,"created":"2026-02-25T17:59:35Z","updated":"2026-04-07T02:57:04Z","license":"MIT","branch":"main","homepage":"https://ebalderasr.github.io/PulseGrowth/","topics":["browser-based","doubling-time","feed-calculation","glucose-uptake","glutamine-uptake","growth-kinetics","ivcd","lab-calculations","mammalian-cell-culture","pwa","specific-growth-rate"],"demo":"https://ebalderasr.github.io/PulseGrowth/","color":"#193546","ink":"#a6d6e8","lastCheckedAt":"2026-10-15T21:46:17.751Z","lastAttemptAt":"2026-10-15T21:46:17.751Z","lastAvailableAt":"2026-10-15T21:46:17.751Z","metrics":[{"at":"2026-10-15T21:46:17.751Z","stars":0,"forks":0}],"technologies":[],"overview":{"kind":"readme","version":1,"paragraphs":["PulseGrowth is a browser-based kinetics calculator for mammalian cell culture. It converts routine two-point sampling data into the growth and metabolic metrics needed for passaging decisions, clone comparisons, and feeding corrections.","The app is organized into three modules: growth kinetics (μ, doubling time, IVCD), specific metabolite consumption rates (qGlc, qGln), and a simple feed correction estimator. All three are designed for quick bench-side use during culture operations.","No installation. No server. Runs entirely in the browser."],"features":["μ and doubling time must be derived manually from a logarithmic expression","Specific rates require IVCD normalization, which is rarely computed at the bench","Unit conversions (g/L → mM) are applied inconsistently, making q values incomparable across runs","Feed correction volumes must be calculated separately from a different formula"],"sourceUrl":"https://github.com/ebalderasr/PulseGrowth/blob/main/README.md","fingerprint":"1cb4de7773f14fe8